.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt NQCHKX 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqchkx
.Nd check a capsule, partially or with its inputs
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Bd -literal
typedef struct {
  const uint8_t *trust;
  size_t trustlen;
  const uint8_t *const *anc;
  const size_t *anclen;
  size_t nanc;
  const char *const *only;
  size_t nonly;
  const char *const *lin;
  size_t nlin;
  const char *const *stmt;
  const size_t *stmtlen;
  size_t nstmt;
} nqcopt;
.Ed
.Pp
.Ft int
.Fn nqchkx "const char *dir" "const nqcopt *o" "nqrep **rep"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqchkx
is
.Xr nqchkt 3
with the options in
.Fa o ;
any member may be 0 or
.Dv NULL ,
and
.Fa o
itself may be
.Dv NULL .
.Fa trust ,
.Fa anc ,
.Fa anclen
and
.Fa nanc
are as for
.Xr nqchkt 3 .
.Pp
.Fa only Ns Bq 0..nonly
makes the check partial: the seal, the signature and the manifest are
checked in full, but only these listed paths are checked as files; the
others are neither read nor needed, and files present but not listed are
not looked for.
.Ql partial
rows say what was left out.
A path the manifest does not list fails its
.Ql file
row.
.Pp
.Fa lin Ns Bq 0..nlin
are folders of capsules that may be the inputs of a format 2 capsule
.Pq Xr nqseal2 3 .
Each input is found among them by its id
.Pq Xr nqcapid 3
and checked in full with no key pinned, its own inputs in turn, to 64
levels; one
.Ql lineage
row per input says whether it was found and checks, and for one that does
not check, its first failing row.
.Pp
.Fa stmt
and
.Fa stmtlen
are reserved for key statements: with
.Fa nstmt
not 0,
.Fn nqchkx
returns
.Er NQENOSUP
and no report.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
As
.Xr nqchk 3 :
.Dv NQOK
when every check passed,
.Er NQEVRFY
when one failed (the report says which),
.Er NQEARG
and
.Er NQEMEM
with no report.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr nqchk 3 ,
.Xr nqchkt 3 ,
.Xr nqprove 3 ,
.Xr nqrep 3 ,
.Xr nqseal2 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
